---
// How it works — three numbered steps in a single horizontal row.
// Keeps the page short and skimmable; deeper content lives in the spec.
---
<section id="how" class="section how">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">how it works</p>
    <h2>Three pieces. That's the whole spec.</h2>

    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <div class="steps__num">01</div>
        <h3>Handshake the vocab.</h3>
        <p>
          Client and server agree on which tokenizer to speak before any token
          ID crosses the wire. Vocabularies are versioned and content-addressed
          via <a href="https://github.com/wdunn001/codec-maps" rel="noopener">codec-maps</a>.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="steps__num">02</div>
        <h3>Stream <code>uint32</code>.</h3>
        <p>
          Token IDs go directly on the wire as 32-bit big-endian integers. No
          JSON envelope, no UTF-8 round-trip, no per-message structural
          overhead. Four bytes per token, every token.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="steps__num">03</div>
        <h3>Frame with control words.</h3>
        <p>
          The high byte of each word distinguishes data from control. Roles,
          tool calls, completion boundaries, and stream resets ride in-band as
          reserved control IDs. One framing layer covers everything.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .steps {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
  @media (min-width: 820px) {
    .steps { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
  }
  .steps li {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.5rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--bg-elev);
  }
  .steps__num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--data);
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    margin-bottom: 0.875rem;
  }
  .steps li h3 { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .steps li code {
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 0.05rem 0.3rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 0.85em;
  }
  .steps li a { color: var(--data); border-bottom: 1px dotted var(--border-strong); }
  .steps li a:hover { border-bottom-color: var(--data); }
</style>
